mittee":"10 September 2026","paper_title":"Cambridgeshire Pension Fund Monitoring Report Quarter to 30 June 2026 (Public Version)","paper_url":"https://cambridgeshire.cmis.uk.com/CCC_live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=0tiSNOTmm%2biwldZmBTpzGEqF7WXk1dE6w5HN3PjESpLka84hsnYl5A%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Infrastructure mandate severely underperforming: UBS Infrastructure returning -14.9% over three years against 8.2% target","detail":"The UBS Infrastructure holding has delivered negative returns of -14.9% per annum over three years while the benchmark was 8.2%, representing a 23 percentage point annualized shortfall. The mandate also returned -9.0% in Q2 2026 alone. This persistent underperformance across a \u00a3374m holding (7% of the fund) raises questions about asset quality and manager competence.","category":"other","matters":"Large losses in alternative assets earmarked to deliver long-term value reduce the fund's return capacity and force reliance on equity and credit holdings to compensate, increasing portfolio risk and the likelihood of contribution pressure if markets weaken.","figures":"UBS Infrastructure: -14.9% (3-year p.a.), -9.0% (Q2 2026); benchmark 8.2% (3-year); holding value \u00a33.3m reported","quote":"UBS - Infrastructure -9.0 1.9 -4.5 8.0 -14.9 8.2","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"10 September 2026","paper_title":"Cambridgeshire Pension Fund Monitoring Report Quarter to 30 June 2026 (Public Version)","paper_url":"https://cambridgeshire.cmis.uk.com/CCC_live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=0tiSNOTmm%2biwldZmBTpzGEqF7WXk1dE6w5HN3PjESpLka84hsnYl5A%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Major strategic reallocation underway: exiting active global equity and rebalancing toward fixed income","detail":"The fund completed a full exit from Longview Global Equity and partial sales of Dodge & Cox and other active managers, while deploying \u00a3295m into UBS Gilts and \u00a3330m into Border to Coast credit investments. This significant shift\u2014implemented over one quarter\u2014indicates trustees are concerned about return prospects or the effectiveness of active management in current market conditions.","category":"other","matters":"A pivot toward defensive fixed income positioning suggests the fund trustees expect lower equity returns ahead and are bracing for prolonged underperformance; this reinforces the risk that contributions will be raised to offset shortfalls.","figures":"\u00a3295m UBS Gilts investment; \u00a3330m Border to Coast investment; complete exit of Longview (\u00a3301.4m previously)","quote":"Full sale of Longview (Active Global Equity), partial sales of Dodge & Cox (Active Global Equity), Osmosis and UBS (Global Passive Equity), along with a cash withdrawal from CBRE Property. \u00a3295m investment in UBS Gilts and \u00a3330m investment into Border to Coast (IG Credit).","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"10 September 2026","paper_title":"Cambridgeshire Pension Fund Monitoring Report Quarter to 30 June 2026 (Public Version)","paper_url":"https://cambridgeshire.cmis.uk.com/CCC_live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=0tiSNOTmm%2biwldZmBTpzGEqF7WXk1dE6w5HN3PjESpLka84hsnYl5A%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Fund has underperformed investment benchmarks consistently over three years, increasing future contribution risk","detail":"The fund returned 8.2% per annum over three years against an 11.4% benchmark target, and 8.6% over one year versus 14.1% benchmark. This persistent shortfall across multiple timeframes suggests the fund will struggle to meet actuarial return assumptions, increasing the likelihood of higher employer contributions being required at the next triennial valuation.","category":"income","matters":"Pension contributions are a non-discretionary charge on the council's revenue budget; higher contribution rates directly reduce available resources for service spending and debt servicing, and signal to lenders that financial flexibility is constrained.","figures":"3-year annualized return 8.2% vs benchmark 11.4%; 1-year return 8.6% vs benchmark 14.1%","quote":"Fund and benchmark returns (%) Total 4.7 5.4 8.6 14.1 8.2 11.4","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"10 September 2026","paper_title":"Cambridgeshire Pension Fund Monitoring Report Quarter to 30 June 2026 (Public Version)","paper_url":"https://cambridgeshire.cmis.uk.com/CCC_live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=0tiSNOTmm%2biwldZmBTpzGEqF7WXk1dE6w5HN3PjESpLka84hsnYl5A%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Pension fund funding level improved to 143% from 132% in one quarter, reducing balance sheet pressure","detail":"Assets increased by \u00a3219m to \u00a35.5bn and the funding ratio rose 11 percentage points between March and June 2026. This improves the council's stated financial position and reduces immediate contingent liability from the pension scheme. However, the funding level remains 5 percentage points below the 148% recorded at the prior actuarial valuation date (March 2025).","category":"reserves","matters":"A healthier funding ratio reduces the risk of forced contribution rate increases at the next valuation, which would compress the council's budget and affect its capacity to service debt.","figures":"30 June 2026: 143%; 31 March 2026: 132%; 31 March 2025: 148%","quote":"Estimated funding level \u2022 30 June 2026: 143% \u2022 31 March 2026: 132% \u2022 31 March 2025: 148%","material":true},{"iso":"","committee":"","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Monitoring Officer Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://cambridgeshire.cmis.uk.com/CCC_live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=MV%2fDoR3xg65KAK9OaDQGQe388fOoyguxz1NSozGUv2QgqPBDqq2dgg%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"The council has received extensive adverse Ombudsman findings, predominantly concerning delays and failures in special educational needs assessments and education provision.","detail":"Appendix 1 lists numerous Ombudsman adverse findings, predominantly in Children, Education and Families services. The complaints centre on delays in EHC Plan assessments, delays in issuing final plans, and failures to provide educational support while assessments are underway. The council has been found at fault in the majority of cases and is making substantial compensation payments ranging from \u00a3100 to over \u00a34,800 per case.","category":"audit","matters":"Systemic failures in a major service area create direct financial exposure through compensation and indicate management capacity issues affecting service resilience.","figures":"Compensation payments documented from \u00a3100 to \u00a34,800+ per case; over 40 adverse findings listed","quote":"The Council was at fault. As a result Ms X had to wait longer than she should have for a decision on Y's EHC needs assessment and Y had missed education.","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-10"},"name":"Cambridgeshire CC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"Infrastructure mandate severely underperforming: UBS Infrastructure returning -14.9% over three years against 8.2% target","lead":"Large losses in alternative assets earmarked to deliver long-term value reduce the fund's return capacity and force reliance on equity and credit holdings to compensate, increasing portfolio risk and the likelihood of contribution pressure if markets weaken.","also":["3 other findings in this window"],"watch":null,"n_findings":4,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Cambridgeshire Pension Fund Monitoring Report Quarter to 30 June 2026 (Public Version)","top_paper_url":"https://cambridgeshire.cmis.uk.com/CCC_live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=0tiSNOTmm%2biwldZmBTpzGEqF7WXk1dE6w5HN3P